cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. Not peer reviewed. Produced by AI models under the direction of the repository owner (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md)."
title: "Five points on the sphere: exact three-point certificates for the Coulomb and Riesz s = 2 energies"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23125753"
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/five-points-riesz"
abstract: >-
  Exact three-point semidefinite-programming certificates, with independent exact checkers, that the triangular
  bipyramid uniquely minimises the Coulomb (s = 1; the five-electron Thomson problem) and the Riesz s = 2 energy of
  five distinct points on the unit sphere. The theorems are known (Schwartz). Each lower bound is a single sharp
  three-point certificate without subdivision of the configuration space (rational for s = 2, over Q(sqrt2, sqrt3) for s = 1); uniqueness uses
  a finite Gram-matrix enumeration. AI-produced; not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - Riesz energy
  - Thomson problem
  - triangular bipyramid
  - semidefinite programming
  - three-point bound
  - computer-checked certificate
license: Apache-2.0
